{
  "name": "devc-vscode",
  "displayName": "Dev Container File Tree",
  "description": "Browse and edit files inside a running dev container (devcontainer CLI / Docker) from VS Code running on the host.",
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "https://github.com/devc-tools/devc-vscode.git"
  },
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "engines": {
    "vscode": "^1.138.0"
  },
  "categories": [
    "Other"
  ],
  "activationEvents": [
    "onFileSystem:devc-vscode",
    "onFileSystem:devc-ssh",
    "onStartupFinished"
  ],
  "main": "./out/extension.js",
  "contributes": {
    "configuration": {
      "title": "Dev Container File Tree",
      "properties": {
        "devc-vscode.dockerPath": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "docker",
          "description": "Docker CLI command used to talk to containers (a name on PATH or an absolute path)."
        },
        "devc-vscode.openFolderCommand": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "devc herdr",
          "description": "Command sent to the terminal by \"Open Folder in Container\" and by the Sandboxes view's Attach Terminal action. Without devc on PATH and with this setting unset, Attach Terminal opens a docker exec shell instead, attached to the container's herdr when it has one."
        },
        "devc-vscode.herdrAttachCommand": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "devc herdr",
          "description": "Command that opens a terminal attached to herdr in the dev container. Run in a new terminal when a herdr agent in the Agents view is clicked and no terminal is showing herdr. Without devc on PATH and with this setting unset, a running container gets a docker exec shell attached to its herdr instead."
        },
        "devc-vscode.agentKinds": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "default": [
            "claude",
            "copilot",
            "pi"
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "Agents offered by the Agents view's Add Agent action, as herdr `--kind` values (see `herdr agent start --help`)."
        },
        "devc-vscode.herdrSession": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "",
          "scope": "window",
          "markdownDescription": "Host herdr session that belongs to this window: the Agents view shows it even with no agents, and attaches to it. Empty uses the name `herdrs` gives the workspace file's directory, or the first folder: its path under your home folder with folders joined by `.`, e.g. `code.tools.devc-vscode` for `~/code/tools/devc-vscode`."
        },
        "devc-vscode.stopCommand": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "devc stop",
          "description": "Command run from a container's host folder by the Agents view's Stop Container action, after its terminals are closed. The action shows when devc is on PATH or this setting is set."
        },
        "devc-vscode.downCommand": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "devc down",
          "description": "Command run from a container's host folder by the Agents view's Down Container action, after its terminals are closed. The action shows when devc is on PATH or this setting is set."
        },
        "devc-vscode.sshHosts": {
          "type": "array",
          "scope": "application",
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "host"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "host": {
                "type": "string",
                "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$"
              },
              "root": {
                "type": "string",
                "pattern": "^/"
              },
              "label": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          "markdownDescription": "SSH hosts offered as environments: file tree roots, Add Agent targets and terminals. `host` is an alias from `~/.ssh/config`; `root` is the absolute remote directory files, terminals and agents start in (default: the remote home). User settings only — use **Add SSH Host…** to pick from `~/.ssh/config`."
        },
        "devc-vscode.sshPath": {
          "type": "string",
          "scope": "application",
          "default": "ssh",
          "description": "ssh client used for SSH environments (a name on PATH or an absolute path). User settings only."
        },
        "devc-vscode.featureFolders": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "scope": "window",
          "markdownDescription": "Turns on **Focus Features…**, **Focus on Active Agents** and **Add Active herdr Space to Workspace**, which add and remove workspace folders and open and close their repositories in Source Control. A repository closed this way stays closed in this workspace until **Git: Reopen Closed Repositories…**."
        },
        "devc-vscode.windowTitle": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "default": null,
          "scope": "window",
          "markdownDescription": "The window title while herdr's focused pane in the dev container is working in a Git repo or worktree. `${branch}` is its branch (the folder name for a detached HEAD), `${project}` the repo's folder name, `${folder}` the worktree's folder name, `${space}` the herdr space's label and `${title}` the title the pane's program sets (what an agent is doing), empty when it only repeats the pane's name or folder. Put `${separator}` around `${title}` so the separator is dropped while it is empty. Anything else, such as `${rootNameShort}`, is one of `#window.title#`'s own variables. Applies only to a saved `.code-workspace`, whose `window.title` setting is rewritten as focus moves. Off (`null`) by default; set it, for example to `${branch} (${rootNameShort})`, to turn it on."
        },
        "devc-vscode.devcWebDevc": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "installed",
          "scope": "window",
          "examples": [
            "installed",
            "devc2"
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "Which devc runs the extension's `devc web`, as devc-desktop's `desktopDevc` picks it: `installed` (devc in `~/.local/bin` or on PATH), `devc2` (the devc-tools checkout from source, through `$DEVC_BIN`, which sourcing devc-tools' `scripts/bash_aliases.sh` exports; read from VS Code's environment, else your login shell's) or an absolute path to a devc binary. Every window shares one `devc web`, so the window that starts it decides. Applies on the next start or **Restart devc web**. Can be set per workspace, which takes effect only in a trusted workspace."
        },
        "devc-vscode.devcWebPort": {
          "type": "integer",
          "default": 48229,
          "minimum": 1,
          "maximum": 65535,
          "scope": "application",
          "markdownDescription": "The port of the one `devc web` every VS Code window shares for the **devc web** view and **Open devc web Tiles**. It is started by the first window that needs it and stopped about 10 seconds after the last window using it closes. Not devc web's own default (48228), so it doesn't clash with a `devc web` you run yourself. Applies on the next start or **Restart devc web**."
        },
        "devc-vscode.devcWebArgs": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "default": [],
          "scope": "window",
          "markdownDescription": "Extra arguments after `devc web --no-open --port <devcWebPort>` for the `devc web` the extension starts for the **devc web** view and **Open devc web Tiles**, for example `[\"--live\", \"--source\", \"/path/to/devc-tools/devc\"]`. A `--port` here replaces `#devc-vscode.devcWebPort#`. Every window shares one `devc web`, so the window that starts it decides. Applies on the next start or **Restart devc web**. Can be set per workspace, which takes effect only in a trusted workspace."
        }
      }
    },
    "commands": [
      {
        "command": "devc-vscode.refresh",
        "title": "Refresh Container Files",
        "category": "Dev Container FS",
        "icon": "$(refresh)"
      },
      {
